# Multi-platform Video Downloader Backend

This backend uses `yt-dlp` instead of relying on a few Cobalt API mirrors.

## Endpoints

- `GET /` - health/status
- `GET /api/health` - health check
- `POST /api/info` with `{ "url": "..." }` - metadata and available formats
- `GET /api/info?url=...` - same as above
- `POST /api/download` with `{ "url": "...", "format_id": "..." }` - server-side download
- `GET /api/download?url=...&format_id=...` - server-side download

## Install

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
python app.py
```

For YouTube formats that require video/audio merging, install FFmpeg on the server and make sure `ffmpeg` is on PATH.

## Frontend

The frontend should call `/api/info` first. For the actual download button, call `/api/download` with the same URL and optionally the selected `format_id`.

## Important

No downloader can honestly guarantee every URL on every platform forever. Platforms change their APIs, login requirements, anti-bot systems, geo restrictions, and media delivery. This backend uses yt-dlp's maintained extractors, which is much more appropriate for a multi-platform downloader than a small hard-coded list of third-party API mirrors.
